/-!
# Binary projective-plane parabolic models

The linear model identifies the concrete projective group with SL₃(2),
and the incidence model describes its seven points and seven lines in
binary coordinates. The two maximal overgroups of each Sylow two-subgroup
are its point and line parabolics. Their coset geometry is equivariantly the
Fano plane, with faithful primitive degree-seven actions. Both parabolics
have elementary four-group cores with faithful irreducible S₃ quotients;
the ambient two-core is trivial. These supply the concrete binary linear
model facts used in Aschbacher–Smith I.5.3–9.
-/
